# Production citation seeding

When the user asks how to seed (or sync) citations on production / the VPS / `citations-server`, read and follow:

`server/docs/production-seeding.md`

Default ops command after deploying **appended** seed JSON (new IDs only):

```bash
docker exec citations-server node dist/scripts/seed-citations.js --sync
```

When `bible-hy.json` was **replaced** and old bible rows must go (after deploy):

```bash
docker exec citations-postgres psql -U citations -d citations -c "DELETE FROM citations WHERE category = 'bible';"
docker exec citations-server node dist/scripts/seed-citations.js --sync
```

Empty DB is seeded automatically on container boot; `--sync` adds new IDs only and does not delete.